From: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bind fbcon to linlondp framebuffer instead of EFI VGA

On Orion O6, UEFI hands off a 1920x1080 simplefb at 0x84800000 which
the kernel registers as fb0 via efifb. Once linlondp probes (~+1s) it
creates fb1 backed by the real DP controller and drives the actual
monitor (e.g. 2560x1440 on DP04). However fbcon stays bound to fb0,
so the console writes go to the obsolete EFI scanout buffer that no
longer reaches any physical display, leaving the monitor blank even
though the DP link is trained.

Disable the EFI framebuffer driver so linlondp becomes fb0 and fbcon
binds to it automatically. Loss: no kernel boot messages on the
monitor before linlondp probes (~1s) - serial console (UART2) and
dmesg still capture everything.

Signed-off-by: Radxa Sky1 <linux-sky1@radxa.com>
---
 src/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/src/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -879,6 +879,5 @@ CONFIG_DRM_TIDSS=m
 CONFIG_FB=y
 CONFIG_FB_MODE_HELPERS=y
-CONFIG_FB_EFI=y
 CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_PWM=m
 CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_LP855X=m
 CONFIG_LOGO=y
